    explanation: "Only an actual restore proves that the backup media, catalog, encryption keys, and restore procedures all work together to return usable data, which is why periodic test restores are the accepted verification control and the evidence auditors request. Reviewing more job logs simply extends the same weak assurance, because a job can report success while writing unusable, incomplete, or unreadable data. Increasing backup frequency reduces potential data loss between copies but does nothing to confirm that any copy can be read back. Replicating the repository to a second array improves availability and protects against a single storage failure, yet it faithfully duplicates corrupt or incomplete backups just as readily as good ones.",
