    explanation: "The Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) is the open, vendor-neutral framework that produces a numeric severity score (0.0 to 10.0) from metrics such as attack vector, complexity, privileges required, and impact to confidentiality, integrity, and availability, which is precisely what is needed to rank remediation work. The Common Platform Enumeration (CPE) is a naming scheme for identifying hardware, operating systems, and applications, not a severity measure. Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) provides a unique identifier and short description for each publicly known vulnerability so that different tools can refer to the same flaw, but a CVE identifier carries no score of its own. Common Configuration Enumeration (CCE) assigns identifiers to system configuration settings for use in benchmarks and compliance checks, again with no severity rating attached.",
