    answer: 0,
    explanation: "User acceptance testing is correct because it is performed by the intended business users, against real business processes, to decide whether the delivered system satisfies the agreed requirements and can be accepted for production use. Unit testing is a developer activity that exercises individual functions in isolation and is completed long before business users are involved. Static analysis examines source code without executing it, looking for insecure patterns and defects, so it involves no user interaction with a running system at all. Stress testing deliberately drives the system beyond its expected load to find its breaking point and observe how it fails, which measures resilience and capacity rather than requirement satisfaction. Security requirements should be represented in acceptance criteria as well, so that a system failing a security requirement can be rejected on the same basis as one failing a functional requirement.",
