    id: "d3_263", domain: 3, difficulty: 2, section: "Memory Protection",
    question: "A vendor states that its compiler and runtime now restrict indirect calls and returns so that execution can only transfer to targets that appear in a statically computed set of valid destinations. Which class of exploitation technique is this specifically intended to defeat?",
